Minimum data requirements: With shared elasticities and domain-specific intercepts, the model requires at least 10–15 domain-year observations per domain to estimate the shared parameters, plus sufficient within-domain variation to identify domain-specific parameters. The Montreal Protocol case provides approximately 40 years of data (1985–2025); COVID provides 3–4 years; the AI governance case provides 3 years. This is insufficient for reliable estimation in the AI domain alone. The strategy is to pool across domains with domain-specific effects, treating the AI case as one of several.

Pre-registration: The hypothesis  \Gamma > 1 + k \cdot (\sigma^2_{PAD} - \sigma^2_{GVCR})/d\ln(PAD)/dt  and the parameter classification above should be pre-registered before estimation.

11.2 Research phases

Phase I — Formalization and Codebook: Complete variable codebook with latent variable estimation for  P, A, D, G, V, C, R . Estimate factor loadings from available data. This phase is the current bottleneck.

Phase II — Historical Calibration: Montreal Protocol as primary case; Cuban Missile Crisis, COVID-19, and AI governance lag as secondary cases. Estimate shared elasticities from pooled data. Test whether the correction loop model explains observed outcomes.

Phase III — Agent-Based Simulation: Heterogeneous agents (states, firms, scientific institutions, AI agents, infrastructure) with coupling and delay. Test whether correction mechanisms prevent catastrophic cascades under varying  K  and  R_{\text{eff}} .

Phase IV — Adversarial AI Stress Tests: Multiple AI systems independently search for hidden failure modes, contradictory assumptions, and measurement problems. Pre-register the search protocol.

Phase V — Earth–Moon–Mars Model: Introduce spatial redundancy with the Autonomy Ladder. Measure whether effective civilizational risk decreases as nodes progress from S0 to S3+.

Phase VI — Empirical Validation: Compare model predictions with observed data. If the theory fails, modify or reject the model rather than protecting it.

